  1. The existing #195 regression suite executes without needing label rewrites for the new output shape.
       inputs:  Use the existing #195 regression corpus exactly as-is, with the new requirement-major decomposition/reporting path enabled, and compare the delivered labels/identifiers against the suite’s current expected labels without any rebinding from source text. The input must be byte-identical #195 cases so a label-rewrite implementation diverges immediately.
       detects: The implementation rebuilds or rewrites #195 labels to fit the new output shape instead of letting the existing regression suite run unchanged.
       full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion obligation-regression-suite-195-unchanged-runs
  2. Each case in the #195 suite keeps the same pass/fail outcome after the change.
       inputs:  Run the full existing #195 suite before and after the change on the same corpus, with the same revisions pinned, and compare per-case pass/fail outcomes. Include cases that were previously near the recall boundary so a flip would be observable if the change perturbs behavior.
       detects: A case in the #195 suite flips result after the update, indicating the representational change altered behavior rather than only output shape.
       full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion obligation-regression-suite-195-results-stable

